17] [17592186083468 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083468 #edb/ref 1045 "Absolute Value Graphs" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083468 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186084061 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083468 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049474 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083468 #edb/ref 1050 420.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083468 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "da88a97d-6c4e-5299-b921-71200664bd9d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084061 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186084062 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084061 #edb/ref 1061 169443 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084061 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "bdb8f706-56c3-508a-a745-c4cf4b268e01" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084061 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186084526 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084062 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186084063 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084062 #edb/ref 1061 169444 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084062 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "6d0878f5-845c-5163-b1ae-e72f37806b6d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084062 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186083189 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084063 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186084064 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084063 #edb/ref 1061 169447 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084063 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "dfd03723-b5ce-5ca8-98bb-2b1cf56700d6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084063 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186083190 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084064 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186084065 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084064 #edb/ref 1061 169450 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084064 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3287422a-9367-5f91-9957-0152a7e772df" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084064 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186084528 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084065 #edb/ref 1061 169451 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084065 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "09be9587-52a8-510c-841a-fe31ae2eb30e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084065 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186083191 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084526 #edb/ref 1064 "Let's plot the graph of ![](images/e3/e31f27c483c52d7933201e37d1f6020c20d7903402be16f28ffd407c7f3db93a.svg). According to the algebraic definition of absolute value, we have\n![](images/eb/ebc6cc8f3964043ffa2ff15f7e3501222794753f30577e4b71037efb2e4ffa30.svg)\nSo, the left-hand branch of the graph is the function ![](images/8f/8f96aa73ce843c7815a1fed6bf3f3774a173cfa4d56f13e1f3a8c48d53cd7097.svg), and the right-hand branch is ![](images/23/238e977be23f692486c8bf68f6b40255435b3d1796cc50d260a014a8c670be7b.svg):\n\n![](images/60/60ad4dfdb6086f20f5137c5b4ac4905e55d5697ec4cf31575bf79be5fd408e0c.png)\n\nNotice that the graph has a sharp corner at ![](images/c1/c1e8c20213b45135f50bdc8d4544220f7b0f943ff3ca49439660c86d017e789f.svg) We call this point the **vertex** or the **minimum point.**\n\nWe can apply **horizontal** and **vertical translations** to the graph of ![](images/e3/e31f27c483c52d7933201e37d1f6020c20d7903402be16f28ffd407c7f3db93a.svg).\n\n- The graph of ![](images/91/91c9b5c48d46f81336e889febab90a9027a96accef8626bd0743ca81042f25b8.svg) is a **vertical translation** of the absolute value graph ![](images/0c/0cb4d1ae0c2e2451edd095b9dbcca94222e8ef0514db46745a2acce4b617d78e.svg) It moves the graph ![](images/34/349015631ec44ef653936c85586d2c5ef56ba64392b3f92b4b92cbef3e731bc5.svg) units up.\n\n![](images/cd/cd8b826034f7c3668cacb490e0fab60daaf7c5cae63975bfa5cae9d468c7dec6.png)\n\n- The graph of ![](images/30/3016548be8be38ace3450d51a10371543820a3357b1adbf809d69c23c70f14bb.svg) is a **horizontal translation** of the absolute value graph ![](images/0c/0cb4d1ae0c2e2451edd095b9dbcca94222e8ef0514db46745a2acce4b617d78e.svg) It moves the graph ![](images/34/349015631ec44ef653936c85586d2c5ef56ba64392b3f92b4b92cbef3e731bc5.svg) units to the *right*.\n\n![](images/65/65912d2831dd525964b78a20f2a707d7d828daa2a5e2ebd0793c6b337a42e360.png)\n\nNote the following:\n\n- When drawing horizontal and vertical translations, it is easiest to transform the graph's vertex first. Then, the two branches can be drawn coming out of the vertex.\n\n- When we translate the graph ![](images/87/87f4b5227cb69bd468d75d826fe448c91ae677181f9142fcbe9bc757d0acea77.svg) the resulting curve is called the **image** of ![](images/e3/e31f27c483c52d7933201e37d1f6020c20d7903402be16f28ffd407c7f3db93a.svg) under the translation." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084526 #edb/ref 1065 9295 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084526 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "1b8dce6a-8742-581b-80f6-e39c9943b395" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084526 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084528 #edb/ref 1064 "Horizontal and vertical translations can be combined. It does not matter which we do first.\n\nIn general, the graph of $y=|x-h|+k$ is a translation of the graph $y=|x|$ by\n\n- $h$ units right, and\n\n- $k$ units up." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084528 #edb/ref 1065 9302 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084528 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "b55739df-8b0d-5ef2-9702-d56de0246597" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084528 #edb/ref 1067 "Combining Translations" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
